    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters May 5th with a clear top-tier quartet, headlined by **Seiya Suzuki** (69.51) and **Corbin Carroll** (69.14). **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Andrew Abbott, where the combination of the pitcher's slow delivery and favorable platoon splits maximizes his stolen base upside\u2014a critical factor for our roster construction. Similarly, **James Wood** (69.03) offers immense value from the leadoff spot; his 0.377 xwOBA is the bedrock of his elite rating, and he is well-positioned to capitalize on a favorable SP skill matchup against Taj Bradley. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.53) rounds out our strongest plays, leveraging a significant platoon advantage against the right-handed Gavin Williams to provide consistent production at 1B.\n\nStrategic positioning is vital today given the scarcity of our target categories. While **Josh Naylor** (63.24) and **Trevor Story** (60.77) are locked into the middle of the order, we are closely monitoring the bottom of the lineup. **Tyler Soderstrom** (45.91) remains a marginal play, though his score was bolstered by an unexpected wind-out factor that barely kept him above the floor. **Jose Caballero** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; his 41.62 score fell just short of our threshold, as the optimizer ultimately penalized his late batting order position and the daunting prospect of facing Jacob deGrom, which suppressed his stolen base efficiency. Meanwhile, we have officially benched **Mickey Moniak** due to an early rainout confirmation, effectively removing any potential for late-game volatility from his roster spot. We are avoiding exposure to **Luis Campusano** and **Alex Freeland**, as both failed to clear the 40.0 efficiency floor required to warrant a start in today\u2019s rotation.",
